---
import InfoPageLayout from '../layouts/InfoPageLayout.astro';
import { VIDEO_GAME_JSON_LD } from '../siteMeta';

const title = 'Mystery Emblem: A Pokemon x Fire Emblem Fan Game You Can Play in Your Browser';
const description =
  'Mystery Emblem is a free Pokemon Fire Emblem fan game: grid tactics in the style of Fire Emblem, with Pokemon Mystery Dungeon pixel art. No download, plays on phone and PC.';
---

<InfoPageLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  heading="About Mystery Emblem"
  jsonLd={[VIDEO_GAME_JSON_LD]}
>
  <figure class="info-figure">
    <img
      src="/boxart.webp"
      width="1024"
      height="572"
      alt="Mystery Emblem box art overlooking the realms and mountains"
      decoding="async"
    />
  </figure>

  <p>
    <strong>Mystery Emblem</strong> is a free <strong>Pokemon x Fire Emblem fan game</strong>. It plays
    like a classic Fire Emblem tactics RPG (move your team across a grid, plan every attack, and
    protect your leader) and looks like <strong>Pokemon Mystery Dungeon: Explorers of Sky</strong>,
    with pixel-art sprites, emotion portraits, and the familiar blue menu windows.
  </p>
  <p>
    It runs right in your web browser on phone, tablet, or PC. There is nothing to download or
    install, and the current playable Act 1 campaign takes under an hour to finish.
  </p>

  <h2>What kind of game is it?</h2>
  <p>
    A turn-based <strong>strategy RPG</strong>. On your turn you move each Pokemon and choose an attack,
    a heal, or an item. Then the enemy moves. Pokemon types replace Fire Emblem's weapon triangle, and
    Pokemon moves take the place of swords, lances, and magic: physical moves strike up close, and
    special moves hit from range.
  </p>

  <h2>Features</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A short personality quiz, in the spirit of Pokemon Mystery Dungeon, picks your Dragon hero: Axew, Bagon, Gible, Dratini, or Goomy.</li>
    <li>Fire Emblem-style battles with counterattacks, type advantages, status conditions, terrain cover, and boss fights.</li>
    <li>Recruit new Pokemon on your expedition, and evolve your team with Evolution Stones.</li>
    <li>A story told through Mystery Dungeon-style sprite cutscenes with character portraits.</li>
    <li>A world map with main chapters, optional paralogue quests, and Kecleon's traveling shops.</li>
    <li>Sign in with Google to save your progress and continue on any device.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The story</h2>
  <p>
    In an ancient age, the Dragon Kingdom ruled the world in peace until Hoopa tore open a Rift in
    space and time to summon savage Paradox Pokemon. Haxorus, Dragonite, and Goodra spent their final
    strength sealing the Rift and hiding three surviving Dragon Eggs: Dreepy, Deino, and yours. Ages
    later, raised in the Verdant Kingdom alongside Quaxly and Flabebe by the retired Royal Guard
    Quaquaval and Florges, a royal summons from King Serperior launches your expedition across the
    realms. Meet the cast on the <a href="/characters/">Characters</a> page.
  </p>

  <h2>What's in the Act 1 demo</h2>
  <p>
    The current release, <em>Act 1: Expedition to Meet King Serperior</em>, includes the Prologue,
    four story chapters, and Paralogue 1: Lush Prairie. Every playtest helps shape Acts 2 through 5.
  </p>

  <h2>Who made it?</h2>
  <p>
    Mystery Emblem is a passion project by Adam Kenawell, a longtime fan of both series. Development
    updates are posted on the <a href="https://adam.kenawell.family/blog/">blog</a>. New to tactics
    games? Start with <a href="/how-to-play/">How to Play</a>, or check the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a>.
  </p>
</InfoPageLayout>
